e=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 17:55:52','2026-02-18 17:55:52',NULL,NULL),(1622,'Who qualifies for the credit?','who-qualifies-for-the-credit-2',NULL,'<p>Businesses with&nbsp;<strong>W-2 employees</strong>&nbsp;in industries where tipping is customaryΓÇötraditionally&nbsp;<strong>food &amp; beverage / hospitality</strong>, and now (new)&nbsp;<strong>beauty &amp; personal care</strong>&nbsp;under the OBBB changes.</p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 17:55:52','2026-02-18 17:55:52',NULL,NULL),(1623,'What changed for the Beauty & Personal Care industry?','what-changed-for-the-beauty-personal-care-industry-2',NULL,'<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Beauty &amp; personal care businesses became&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">new qualifying businesses after 12/31/24</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, and the credit is&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">claimed with 2025 returns</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, due to the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">2025 Budget Reconciliation Bill (OBBB)</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;signed into law&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">July 4, 2025</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 17:55:52','2026-02-18 17:55:52',NULL,NULL),(1624,'What beauty businesses are typically tipped and may qualify?','what-beauty-businesses-are-typically-tipped-and-may-qualify-2',NULL,'<p><strong>What beauty businesses are typically tipped and may qualify?</strong></p><p>Common examples include:</p><ul><li>Hair salons &amp; barbershops</li><li>Nail salons</li><li>Spas, wellness centers (facials, wraps, body treatments, etc.)</li><li>Esthetics &amp; skincare studios (waxing, lashes, brows, tanning)</li><li>Makeup artists</li><li>Fitness services (trainers / group instructors)&nbsp;<em>(where tipping is standard in that setting)</em></li></ul><p><br></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 17:55:52','2026-02-18 17:55:52',NULL,NULL),(1625,'WhatΓÇÖs the minimum wage threshold for the credit calculation?','whats-the-minimum-wage-threshold-for-the-credit-calculation-2',NULL,'<p>For eligibility and credit math, the ΓÇ£minimum wage basisΓÇ¥ differs by industry:</p><ul><li><strong>Restaurant/hospitality:</strong>&nbsp;<strong>$5.15</strong>&nbsp;(for this creditΓÇÖs calculation rules)</li><li><strong>Beauty/personal care:</strong>&nbsp;<strong>$7.25</strong>&nbsp;(for this creditΓÇÖs calculation rules)</li></ul><p><br></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 17:55:52','2026-02-18 17:55:52',NULL,NULL),(1626,'Is this a refund of payroll taxes?','is-this-a-refund-of-payroll-taxes-2',NULL,'<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">No. The FICA Tip Credit&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">does not refund payroll taxes</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;you already paid. It offsets&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">income tax owed</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;by the business (C-Corp) or flows through to owners (S-Corp/Partnership). Refund outcomes depend on your tax liability and credit utilization rules.</span></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 17:55:52','2026-02-18 17:55:52',NULL,NULL),(1627,'How far back can we recover missed credits?','how-far-back-can-we-recover-missed-credits-2',NULL,'<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Often the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">current year plus up to the last three years</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;(depending on filing timing and amendment rules). After enough time passes, that year is goneΓÇöno rewinds.</span></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 17:55:52','2026-02-18 17:55:52',NULL,NULL),(1628,'How Your Credit Gets Paid (And When Fees Are Charged)','how-your-credit-gets-paid-and-when-fees-are-charged-2',NULL,'<h3><strong>Full Refund</strong></h3><ul><li>You receive a full cash refund</li><li>No fee due at filing</li><li>Fee can be deducted after IRS processes refund (or optional advance)</li></ul><h3><strong> Partial Refund + Partial Carry-Forward</strong></h3><ul><li>Some refunded now, some applied to future taxes</li><li>If refund covers fee ΓåÆ no payment at filing</li><li>If not ΓåÆ invoiced when filed</li><li>Contingency-style when possible</li></ul><h3><strong> Full Carry-Forward</strong></h3><ul><li>Entire credit carries forward to offset future tax years</li><li>Fee is invoiced at filing (financing options available)</li></ul><p><br></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 17:55:52','2026-02-18 17:55:52',NULL,NULL),(1629,'What We Do (And Why It Matters)','what-we-do-and-why-it-matters-2',NULL,'<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">Because this credit is easy to miss, easy to miscalculate, and expensive to ignore. We confirm you qualify, calculate it correctly, file it clean, and support you if the IRS ever asks questions.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>1) Quiet Second Opinion (Eligibility + Real Savings)</strong></p><p>We confirm you qualify under&nbsp;<strong>IRS ┬º45B</strong>, identify which employees/services count, and estimate what you may be missing.</p><p><strong>2) Tip + Payroll Verification (Built to Hold Up)</strong></p><p>We verify tips are captured through payroll and reflected properly in your reporting, since the credit is based on&nbsp;<strong>reported tips</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>employer-paid FICA</strong>.</p><p><strong>3) Tip vs Service Charge Separation (Big Deal)</strong></p><p>We separate true tips from&nbsp;<strong>service charges/auto-gratuities</strong>, because mandatory charges generally donΓÇÖt qualify as tips for the credit.</p><p><strong>4) Minimum Wage Threshold Math (Where People Mess Up)</strong></p><p>We apply the correct minimum-wage basis rules so the credit only includes&nbsp;<strong>eligible tips above the threshold</strong>.</p><p><strong>5) Form 8846-Ready Credit Package</strong></p><p>We prepare the calculations and documentation needed to claim the credit correctly using&nbsp;<strong>Form 8846</strong>.</p><p><strong>6) Prior-Year Recovery (When Eligible)</strong></p><p>We help pursue missed credits for prior years through amended filings, so you stop losing money to the calendar.</p><h3>The ΓÇ£Real TipΓÇ¥ Rules We Check</h3><p>For tips to count, they must be:</p><ul><li><strong>Voluntary</strong>&nbsp;(not forced; service charges generally donΓÇÖt count)</li><li>Customer controls the&nbsp;<strong>amount</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>who receives it</strong></li><li><strong>Reported to the employer</strong></li><li>Earned by&nbsp;<strong>W-2 employees</strong>&nbsp;(not contractors)</li><li>Wages + tips exceed minimum wage</li><li>Credit applies to tips&nbsp;<strong>above</strong>&nbsp;the minimum-wage basis used in the calculation</li></ul><h2>How Our Process Works</h2><p><strong>01 ΓÇö Simple Application</strong></p><p>Quick form with basic business info.</p><p><strong>Transparent Pricing:</strong>&nbsp;no upfront cost to check eligibility; fees explained before you sign.</p><p><strong>02 ΓÇö We Do the Heavy Lifting</strong></p><p>We calculate savings, prepare documents, and handle filing requirements.</p><p><strong>03 ΓÇö Tracking + Audit Defense Included</strong></p><p>We keep you updated and respond with documentation support if the IRS asks questions.</p><p><strong>04 ΓÇö Get Paid</strong></p><h3>Timing varies by IRS processing.&nbsp;<strong>Advance options may be available</strong>&nbsp;for eligible businesses (when offered).</h3>',NULL,NULL,'1',22,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 17:55:52','2026-02-18 17:55:52',NULL,NULL),(1630,'Who is Dan','who-is-danna-2',NULL,'<p>Most firms chase revenue. I go hunting for the money youΓÇÖve already earned and never claimed.</p><p>I work with owners and operators in tip-driven businesses to uncover ΓÇ£hiddenΓÇ¥ cash flow through the&nbsp;<strong>FICA Tips Tax Credit (IRS ┬º45B)</strong>ΓÇöthe dollar-for-dollar credit tied to the&nbsp;<strong>employer-paid FICA</strong>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<strong>employee-reported tips</strong>. That means doing the parts most people skip: validating eligibility, separating&nbsp;<strong>true tips vs. service charges</strong>, applying the&nbsp;<strong>minimum-wage threshold rules</strong>, and making sure the numbers are built to match whatΓÇÖs been reported through payroll so the filing is clean.</p><p>Bottom line: if youΓÇÖve got tipped W-2 employees and youΓÇÖre not filing&nbsp;<strong>Form 8846</strong>&nbsp;each year, thereΓÇÖs a good chance youΓÇÖre missing real savings. I keep it straightforward, explain it in plain English, and focus on outcomesΓÇönot noise. If you want fewer leaks and more money staying where it belongs, IΓÇÖm your guy.</p>',NULL,NULL,'1',16,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 17:55:52','2026-02-19 17:36:16',NULL,NULL),(1631,'Click Here to Join My Team','click-here-to-join-my-team-4',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1',24,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 18:19:47','2026-02-18 18:19:47',NULL,NULL),(1632,'Check My Availability','check-my-availability',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1',14,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 19:19:47','2026-02-18 19:19:47',NULL,NULL),(1633,'Uncle Dan Consulting','uncle-dan-consulting',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1',26,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 19:23:36','2026-02-18 19:23:36',NULL,NULL),(1634,'The FICA Tips Tax Credit: The Money Most Tipped Businesses Miss','the-fica-tips-tax-credit-the-money-most-tipped-businesses-miss',NULL,'<p>If you have&nbsp;<strong>tipped W-2 employees</strong>&nbsp;and youΓÇÖre&nbsp;<strong>not filing Form 8846</strong>, thereΓÇÖs a strong chance youΓÇÖre leaving money on the table.</p><p>The&nbsp;<strong>FICA Tips Tax Credit (IRS ┬º45B)</strong>&nbsp;is an&nbsp;<strong>income tax credit</strong>&nbsp;that lets eligible employers claim back the&nbsp;<strong>employer portion of FICA (7.65%)</strong>&nbsp;paid on&nbsp;<strong>employee-reported tips</strong>. ItΓÇÖs not a payroll refundΓÇöit reduces income tax owed (and depending on your situation, it can create a refund or carry forward).</p><h2>Who typically qualifies?</h2><p>Historically, itΓÇÖs been&nbsp;<strong>restaurants and hospitality</strong>ΓÇöthink:</p><ul><li>Full-service restaurants, bars, nightclubs</li><li>Hotels/resorts, catering, cafes</li><li>Other tip-customary service operations</li></ul><p>And starting&nbsp;<strong>after 12/31/2024</strong>&nbsp;(claimed on&nbsp;<strong>2025 returns</strong>), qualifying&nbsp;<strong>beauty &amp; personal care</strong>&nbsp;businesses with tipped W-2 staff may also qualify.</p><h2>The 4 reasons businesses get it wrong</h2><ol><li><strong>Not all ΓÇ£gratuitiesΓÇ¥ count</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇö service charges/auto-gratuities often donΓÇÖt qualify.</li><li><strong>Minimum wage threshold rules apply</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇö the credit generally applies to eligible tips&nbsp;<strong>above</strong>&nbsp;the threshold used in the calculation.</li><li><strong>Tip reporting must be solid</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇö itΓÇÖs based on&nbsp;<strong>reported tips</strong>&nbsp;and employer FICA paid.</li><li><strong>W-2 employees only</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇö contractors donΓÇÖt qualify.</li></ol><h2>Why it gets missed</h2><p>Payroll companies usually wonΓÇÖt apply it automatically, and many tax preparers donΓÇÖt take the time to calculate it properly. Owners assume itΓÇÖs being handledΓÇª and it often isnΓÇÖt.</p><h2>Bottom line</h2><p>A quick review can tell you if youΓÇÖre missing the credit nowΓÇöand whether prior years may still be recoverable. No hype. Just math.</p>',NULL,'2026-02-18','1',6,1,199,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-18 20:34:03','2026-02-18 20:34:40',NULL,NULL),(1635,'My Mission','my-mission-9',NULL,'<p><strong>My mission is to guide restaurants, hospitality, and qualifying beauty businesses through the FICA Tips Tax Credit process with clarity and integrityΓÇöhelping them claim what theyΓÇÖre owed and build cleaner payroll and reporting systems going forward.</strong></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',19,1,201,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-21 02:41:11','2026-02-21 02:41:11',NULL,NULL),(1636,'What is the FICA Tips Tax Credit?','what-is-the-fica-tips-tax-credit-3',NULL,'<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">ItΓÇÖs an&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">income tax credit</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;that lets eligible employers recover the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">employer-paid FICA (Social Security + Medicare)</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;on&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">employee-reported tips</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">. The rate tied to that employer FICA portion is&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">7.65%</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,201,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-21 02:41:11','2026-02-21 02:41:11',NULL,NULL),(1637,'Who qualifies for the credit?','who-qualifies-for-the-credit-3',NULL,'<p>Businesses with&nbsp;<strong>W-2 employees</strong>&nbsp;in industries where tipping is customaryΓÇötraditionally&nbsp;<strong>food &amp; beverage / hospitality</strong>, and now (new)&nbsp;<strong>beauty &amp; personal care</strong>&nbsp;under the OBBB changes.</p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,201,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-21 02:41:11','2026-02-21 02:41:11',NULL,NULL),(1638,'What changed for the Beauty & Personal Care industry?','what-changed-for-the-beauty-personal-care-industry-3',NULL,'<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Beauty &amp; personal care businesses became&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">new qualifying businesses after 12/31/24</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, and the credit is&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">claimed with 2025 returns</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, due to the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">2025 Budget Reconciliation Bill (OBBB)</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;signed into law&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">July 4, 2025</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,201,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-21 02:41:11','2026-02-21 02:41:11',NULL,NULL),(1639,'What beauty businesses are typically tipped and may qualify?','what-beauty-businesses-are-typically-tipped-and-may-qualify-3',NULL,'<p><strong>What beauty businesses are typically tipped and may qualify?</strong></p><p>Common examples include:</p><ul><li>Hair salons &amp; barbershops</li><li>Nail salons</li><li>Spas, wellness centers (facials, wraps, body treatments, etc.)</li><li>Esthetics &amp; skincare studios (waxing, lashes, brows, tanning)</li><li>Makeup artists</li><li>Fitness services (trainers / group instructors)&nbsp;<em>(where tipping is standard in that setting)</em></li></ul><p><br></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,201,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-21 02:41:11','2026-02-21 02:41:11',NULL,NULL),(1640,'WhatΓÇÖs the minimum wage threshold for the credit calculation?','whats-the-minimum-wage-threshold-for-the-credit-calculation-3',NULL,'<p>For eligibility and credit math, the ΓÇ£minimum wage basisΓÇ¥ differs by industry:</p><ul><li><strong>Restaurant/hospitality:</strong>&nbsp;<strong>$5.15</strong>&nbsp;(for this creditΓÇÖs calculation rules)</li><li><strong>Beauty/personal care:</strong>&nbsp;<strong>$7.25</strong>&nbsp;(for this creditΓÇÖs calculation rules)</li></ul><p><br></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,201,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-21 02:41:11','2026-02-21 02:41:11',NULL,NULL),(1641,'Is this a refund of payroll taxes?','is-this-a-refund-of-payroll-taxes-3',NULL,'<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">No. The FICA Tip Credit&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">does not refund payroll taxes</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;you already paid. It offsets&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">income tax owed</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;by the business (C-Corp) or flows through to owners (S-Corp/Partnership). Refund outcomes depend on your tax liability and credit utilization rules.</span></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,201,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-21 02:41:11','2026-02-21 02:41:11',NULL,NULL),(1642,'How far back can we recover missed credits?','how-far-back-can-we-recover-missed-credits-3',NULL,'<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Often the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">current year plus up to the last three years</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;(depending on filing timing and amendment rules). After enough time passes, that year is goneΓÇöno rewinds.</span></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,201,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-21 02:41:11','2026-02-21 02:41:11',NULL,NULL),(1643,'How Your Credit Gets Paid (And When Fees Are Charged)','how-your-credit-gets-paid-and-when-fees-are-charged-3',NULL,'<h3><strong>Full Refund</strong></h3><ul><li>You receive a full cash refund</li><li>No fee due at filing</li><li>Fee can be deducted after IRS processes refund (or optional advance)</li></ul><h3><strong> Partial Refund + Partial Carry-Forward</strong></h3><ul><li>Some refunded now, some applied to future taxes</li><li>If refund covers fee ΓåÆ no payment at filing</li><li>If not ΓåÆ invoiced when filed</li><li>Contingency-style when possible</li></ul><h3><strong> Full Carry-Forward</strong></h3><ul><li>Entire credit carries forward to offset future tax years</li><li>Fee is invoiced at filing (financing options available)</li></ul><p><br></p>',NULL,NULL,'1',13,1,201,NULL,NULL,'2026-02-21 02:41:11','2026-02-21 02:41:11',NULL,NULL),(1644,'What We Do (And Why It Matters)','what-we-do-and-why-it-matters-3',NULL,'<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(230, 0, 0);\">Because this credit is easy to miss, easy to miscalculate, and expensive to ignore. We confirm you qualify, calculate it correctly, file it clean, and support you if the IRS ever asks questions.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>1) Qu