L.</em></p>',1,194,3,'2026-02-03 01:43:23','2026-02-03 01:43:23'),(1131,'Focus','<p><strong>ΓÇ£I needed help because IΓÇÖm planning a major purchase and didnΓÇÖt want to mess it up. Walter helped me understand what to focus on right now, what to avoid, and how to move smarter.ΓÇ¥</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇö&nbsp;<em>Anthony C.</em></p><p><br></p>',1,194,3,'2026-02-03 01:44:43','2026-02-03 01:44:43'),(1132,'Services','<h3> <strong>Protection Plan (Core Membership)</strong></h3><ul><li>≡ƒº╛&nbsp;<strong>Credit Restoration Support</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇô Help identifying issues and addressing inaccuracies/errors impacting your credit profile.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>≡ƒò╡∩╕Å&nbsp;<strong>Identity Monitoring</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇô Monitor key identity/credit signals to help you catch fraud faster.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>≡ƒÄ»&nbsp;<strong>Savings Goals &amp; Budget Structure</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇô Build a plan that turns ΓÇ£I should saveΓÇ¥ into ΓÇ£itΓÇÖs actually happening.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>≡ƒùé∩╕Å&nbsp;<strong>Financial Lockbox / Organization</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇô Keep important financial documents organized so life doesnΓÇÖt feel like a scavenger hunt.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>≡ƒºá&nbsp;<strong>Net Worth Tracking</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇô Track what you own vs. what you owe and build forward with visibility.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>≡ƒô£&nbsp;<strong>Will &amp; Trust</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇô Tools/resources to help protect your family plans and wishes.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>ΓÜû∩╕Å&nbsp;<strong>Credit Attorney Access (as included/available)</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇô Support options connected to credit matters when applicable.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><h3><strong>≡ƒº╛ TaxTrac (For tax pros + business-minded clients)</strong></h3><ul><li>≡ƒÆ╗&nbsp;<strong>Tax Software Platform</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇô Professional-grade prep software for 1040 federal/state/local returns (all in one platform) + secure client communication.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>≡ƒÅó&nbsp;<strong>Service Bureau Tools</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇô Options for building/operating a tax office model (where applicable).&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><h3><strong>≡ƒÆ│ Credit-Building Tools </strong></h3><ul><li>≡ƒ¬¬&nbsp;<strong>Secured card options</strong>&nbsp;ΓÇô A path some people use to begin establishing/rebuilding credit.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p>',1,195,1,'2026-02-03 17:03:33','2026-02-03 17:03:33'),(1133,'Simple','<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">ΓÇ£Carlos made everything simple. I wasnΓÇÖt embarrassed, I wasnΓÇÖt overwhelmed ΓÇö I finally felt like I had a clear plan instead of guessing every month.ΓÇ¥ ΓÇö</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> Jasmine R.</span></p>',1,195,3,'2026-02-06 00:44:27','2026-02-06 00:44:27'),(1134,'Broke it Down','<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">ΓÇ£What I liked most is Carlos actually listens. He broke things down step-by-step and helped me feel in control of my credit and finances for the first time.ΓÇ¥ </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">ΓÇö Devon M.</span></p>',1,195,3,'2026-02-06 00:45:03','2026-02-06 00:45:03'),(1135,'Patient & Focused','<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">ΓÇ£IΓÇÖve talked to people before who just tried to sell me something. Carlos was different ΓÇö real, patient, and focused on helping me build structure that lasts.ΓÇ¥</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> ΓÇö Monique L.</span></p>',1,195,3,'2026-02-06 00:45:55','2026-02-06 00:45:55'),(1136,'Clarity','<p><strong>ΓÇ£I came in stressed and confused. After one call with Carlos, I had clarity, direction, and confidence. The process was organized and easy to follow.ΓÇ¥ </strong>ΓÇö Anthony S.</p><p><br></p>',1,195,3,'2026-02-06 00:46:39','2026-02-06 00:46:39'),(1137,'Straightforward','<p><strong>ΓÇ£Carlos is knowledgeable but also genuinely cares. He kept it straightforward, answered every question, and made me feel like I had someone in my corner.ΓÇ¥ </strong>ΓÇö Priya K.</p><p><br></p>',1,195,3,'2026-02-06 00:47:30','2026-02-06 00:47:30'),(1138,'FICA Tips Tax Credit Recovery (IRS Code ┬º45B)','<h3><strong>Recover the FICA Tips Tax Credit (Current Year + Up to 3 Prior Years)</strong></h3><p>If you have&nbsp;<strong>tipped W-2 employees</strong>&nbsp;and youΓÇÖre&nbsp;<strong>not filing Form 8846</strong>, thereΓÇÖs a strong chance youΓÇÖre leaving real money behind. We help you recover the&nbsp;<strong>current year</strong>&nbsp;and, when eligible, go back&nbsp;<strong>up to three years</strong>&nbsp;through amended returns.</p><p><br></p><h3>≡ƒì╜∩╕Å<strong> Food &amp; Beverage (The Classic ┬º45B Credit)</strong></h3><p>Restaurants and hospitality businesses have been eligible for decades ΓÇö but most never claim it because payroll providers donΓÇÖt apply it automatically and many preparers donΓÇÖt chase it.</p><p>We handle the full credit calculation using the rules that apply to&nbsp;<strong>food/beverage tipped employees</strong>, including the ΓÇ£non-creditable tipsΓÇ¥ minimum wage basis used in the calculation (Form 8846 instructions reference&nbsp;<strong>$5.15/hour</strong>&nbsp;for food or beverage employees).&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><h3><strong>≡ƒÆç Beauty &amp; Personal Care (New Eligibility After 12/31/24 ΓÇö Claimed on 2025 Returns)</strong></h3><p>As part of the&nbsp;<strong>2025 Budget Reconciliation Bill</strong>&nbsp;(aka the&nbsp;<strong>One Big Beautiful Bill / One Big Beautiful Bill Act</strong>), signed into law&nbsp;<strong>July 4, 2025</strong>, the FICA tip credit was expanded to include&nbsp;<strong>beauty service establishments</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p>The bill language extends ┬º45B to ΓÇ£beauty servicesΓÇ¥ and applies to&nbsp;<strong>tax years beginning after Dec. 31, 2024</strong>&nbsp;(meaning itΓÇÖs claimed with&nbsp;<strong>2025 returns</strong>).&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Beauty services (as defined in the bill / IRS form instructions) include:</strong></p><ul><li>Barbering &amp; hair care</li><li>Nail care</li><li>Esthetics</li><li>Body &amp; spa treatments&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Important beauty-industry qualifier:</strong></p><p>To claim the credit for beauty services, the law adds a threshold:&nbsp;<strong>tips for those services must exceed 15% of gross receipts</strong>&nbsp;for those services in the year.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Beauty minimum wage basis for the credit:</strong>&nbsp;Form 8846 instructions reference&nbsp;<strong>$7.25/hour</strong>&nbsp;for beauty service employees.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><h3><strong>Γ£¿ Qualifying Beauty Businesses Where Tipping Is Standard</strong></h3><p>If tipping is customary and you employ W-2 staff, many of these often fall into the ΓÇ£beauty servicesΓÇ¥ bucket (or contain qualifying services inside the business):</p><ul><li>Hair salons &amp; barbershops (stylists, colorists, barbers, assistants/shampoo staff)</li><li>Nail salons (manicures/pedicures)</li><li>Spas / wellness centers (facials, wraps, body treatments, etc.)</li><li>Esthetics &amp; skincare studios (waxing, lashes, brows, tanning, etc.)</li><li>Makeup artists (studio/event work)</li></ul><p><strong>Note:</strong>&nbsp;Tipping is generally not expected/allowed for medical professionals performing medical procedures (Botox/fillers), but&nbsp;<strong>non-medical services</strong>&nbsp;in the same facility may still involve tips and may qualify depending on service type.</p>',1,196,1,'2026-02-06 02:26:27','2026-02-06 11:01:57'),(1139,'Easily Explained','<p><strong>ΓÇ£Danna was the first person who explained this credit in plain English and then actually did the work. Eligibility, tip rules, documentationΓÇöhandled. We stopped guessing and started filing correctly.ΓÇ¥</strong></p><p>Anthony R., Restaurant Owner ΓÇö Los Angeles, CA</p>',1,196,3,'2026-02-06 11:27:20','2026-02-06 11:27:20'),(1140,'Found What We Missed','<p><strong>ΓÇ£We assumed payroll or our CPA would automatically catch this. Nope. Danna found what we missed, showed us why, and packaged it in a way that felt clean and defensible.ΓÇ¥</strong></p><p>Melissa K.,