ed payroll or our CPA would automatically catch this. Nope. Rob found what we missed, showed us why, and packaged it in a way that felt clean and defensible.ΓÇ¥</strong></p><p>Melissa K., Controller ΓÇöBrookshire, TX</p>',1,201,3,'2026-02-21 02:41:11','2026-02-21 12:23:13'),(1170,'Knows His Craft','<p><strong>ΓÇ£Rob doesnΓÇÖt ΓÇÿkind ofΓÇÖ understand the FICA tip creditΓÇöshe knows it cold. He caught mistakes we didnΓÇÖt even realize mattered and helped us fix them going forward.ΓÇ¥</strong></p><p>Priya S., Hospitality Owner ΓÇö San Francisco, CA</p>',1,201,3,'2026-02-21 02:41:11','2026-02-21 03:42:55'),(1171,'Understands Your Need','<p><strong>ΓÇ£WeΓÇÖre in California and the wage/tip rules can get complicated fast. Rob knew exactly how to navigate it and make sure we only claimed what truly qualified.ΓÇ¥</strong></p><p>Jonathan M., Multi-Location Operator ΓÇö Sacramento, CA</p>',1,201,3,'2026-02-21 02:41:11','2026-02-21 03:27:37'),(1173,'Found What We Were Missing','<p><strong>I honestly thought our payroll company or CPA was already handling the FICA tip credit. They werenΓÇÖt. Robert did a ΓÇ£quiet second opinion,ΓÇ¥ found what we were missing, and explained it in plain English without drowning me in tax speak. He also caught issues around tips vs. service charges that couldΓÇÖve made the filing messy. Super organized, responsive, and the process was way smoother than I expected.</strong></p><p><strong>ΓÇö Anthony R., Brooklyn, NY</strong></p><p><br></p>',1,201,3,'2026-02-21 12:17:07','2026-02-21 12:17:07'),(1174,'Communication Was Solid','<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Robert is the opposite of the ΓÇ£tax hypeΓÇ¥ people. He doesnΓÇÖt promise magicΓÇöhe verifies everything. He reviewed our payroll and tip reporting, confirmed eligibility, and built the credit package clean and defensible. Communication was solid the whole time, and he kept it simple: what he needed, why he needed it, and what the next step was.</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(