>Past credit challenges do not automatically mean you cannot qualify. DriveX Auto offers subprime financing assistance and works with customers who have good credit, challenged credit or little to no established credit history. All approvals remain subject to lender requirements.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><h2><strong>≡ƒöä Trade-In Assistance</strong></h2><p>Have a vehicle to trade? The DriveX Auto team can evaluate your current vehicle and help apply its available value toward your next purchase.</p><h2><strong>≡ƒöì Personalized Vehicle Finder</strong></h2><p>Do not see the exact vehicle you need? Submit your desired year, make, model, mileage, color, features and budget, and the team can assist with the search.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><h2><strong>≡ƒº░ Automotive Service &amp; Repairs</strong></h2><p>DriveX Auto promotes dealership service, expert auto repairs and maintenance for all makes and models. Its social content also promotes routine services such as oil changes.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><h2><strong>≡ƒ¢í∩╕Å Service Contracts &amp; Warranty Options</strong></h2><p>Qualifying vehicles may be eligible for available extended service contracts or warranty products. Coverage, eligibility, exclusions and pricing should be confirmed directly with DriveX Auto before purchase.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><h2><strong>≡ƒÜÜ Pickup &amp; Delivery Coordination</strong></h2><p>Customers can work with the professional sales team to arrange dealership pickup or available vehicle delivery options.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><h2><strong>≡ƒùô∩╕Å Test Drives &amp; Appointments</strong></h2><p>Contact the dealership to check availability, schedule a test drive, discuss financing or arrange a service appointment.</p>',1,218,1,'2026-04-19 07:26:12','2026-07-18 21:15:59'),(1233,'GOOGLE REVIEWS','<h3><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 102, 204);\">Click Here to See Our Reviews</strong></h3>',1,218,3,'2026-04-19 08:27:07','2026-07-18 21:54:22'),(1234,'Aventz Co. Services','<p><strong>Wedding Planning</strong></p><p>Full-service guidance to help couples plan a seamless, thoughtful, and beautifully executed wedding from vision to celebration.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Wedding Design</strong></p><p>Design support that brings together color, d├⌐cor, florals, and styling so the entire wedding feels cohesive, elegant, and personal.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Wedding Management</strong></p><p>Strategic coordination and timeline oversight to make sure every moving part comes together smoothly on the big day.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Event Planning</strong></p><p>Planning services for social affairs, retreats, intimate gatherings, and personalized events handled with care, structure, and creativity.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Event Design</strong></p><p>Thoughtful visual planning and styling that transforms an event into an intentional and memorable experience.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Wedding Weekend Support</strong></p><p>Planning and coordination support beyond the ceremony itself, helping shape the full wedding weekend experience.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Brand Activations &amp; Personalized Events</strong></p><p>Boutique event support for brands and custom experiences that need both visual impact and strong execution.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><h2><br></h2>',1,220,1,'2026-04-22 20:40:45','2026-04-22 20:40:45'),(1235,'Client Testimonials','<p>Click Here to See Reviews</p>',1,220,3,'2026-04-27 18:21:32','2026-04-27 18:22:23'),(1236,'FICA Tips Tax Credit Recovery (IRS Code ┬º45B)','<h3><strong>Recover the FICA Tips Tax Credit (Current Year + Up to 3 Prior Years)</strong></h3><p>If you have&nbsp;<strong>tipped W-2 employees</strong>&nbsp;and youΓÇÖre&nbsp;<strong>not filing Form 8846</strong>, thereΓÇÖs a strong chance youΓÇÖre leaving real money behind. We help you recover the&nbsp;<strong>current year</strong>&nbsp;and, when eligible, go back&nbsp;<strong>up to three years</strong>&nbsp;through amended returns.</p><p><br></p><h3>≡ƒì╜∩╕Å<strong> Food &amp; Beverage (The Classic ┬º45B Credit)</strong></h3><p>Restaurants and hospitality businesses have been eligible for decades ΓÇö but most never claim it because payroll providers donΓÇÖt apply it automatically and many preparers donΓÇÖt chase it.</p><p>We handle the full credit calculation using the rules that apply to&nbsp;<strong>food/beverage tipped employees</strong>, including the ΓÇ£non-creditable tipsΓÇ¥ minimum wage basis used in the calculation (Form 8846 instructions reference&nbsp;<strong>$5.15/hour</strong>&nbsp;for food or beverage employees).&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><h3><strong>≡ƒÆç Beauty &amp; Personal Care (New Eligibility After 12/31/24 ΓÇö Claimed on 2025 Returns)</strong></h3><p>As part of the&nbsp;<strong>2025 Budget Reconciliation Bill</strong>&nbsp;(aka the&nbsp;<strong>One Big Beautiful Bill / One Big Beautiful Bill Act</strong>), signed into law&nbsp;<strong>July 4, 2025</strong>, the FICA tip credit was expanded to include&nbsp;<strong>beauty service establishments</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p>The bill language extends ┬º45B to ΓÇ£beauty servicesΓÇ¥ and applies to&nbsp;<strong>tax years beginning after Dec. 31, 2024</strong>&nbsp;(meaning itΓÇÖs claimed with&nbsp;<strong>2025 returns</strong>).&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Beauty services (as defined in the bill / IRS form instructions) include:</strong></p><ul><li>Barbering &amp; hair care</li><li>Nail care</li><li>Esthetics</li><li>Body &amp; spa treatments&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Important beauty-industry qualifier:</strong></p><p>To claim the credit for beauty services, the law adds a threshold:&nbsp;<strong>tips for those services must exceed 15% of gross receipts</strong>&nbsp;for those services in the year.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Beauty minimum wage basis for the credit:</strong>&nbsp;Form 8846 instructions reference&nbsp;<strong>$7.25/hour</strong>&nbsp;for beauty service employees.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><h3><strong>Γ£¿ Qualifying Beauty Businesses Where Tipping Is Standard</strong></h3><p>If tipping is customary and you employ W-2 staff, many of these often fall into the ΓÇ£beauty servicesΓÇ¥ bucket (or contain qualifying services inside the business):</p><ul><li>Hair salons &amp; barbershops (stylists, colorists, barbers, assistants/shampoo staff)</li><li>Nail salons (manicures/pedicures)</li><li>Spas / wellness centers (facials, wraps, body treatments, etc.)</li><li>Esthetics &amp; skincare studios (waxing, lashes, brows, tanning, etc.)</li><li>Makeup artists (studio/event work)</li></ul><p><strong>Note:</strong>&nbsp;Tipping is generally not expected/allowed for medical professionals performing medical procedures (Botox/fillers), but&nbsp;<strong>non-medical services</strong>&nbsp;in the same facility may still involve tips and may qualify depending on service type.</p>',1,223,1,'2026-04-27 19:59:36','2026-04-27 19:59:36'),(1237,'Easily Explained','<p><strong>ΓÇ£Danna was the first person who explained this credit in plain English and then actually did the work. Eligibility, tip rules, documentationΓÇöhandled. We stopped guessing and started filing correctly.ΓÇ¥</strong></p><p>Anthony R., Restaurant Owner ΓÇö Los Angeles, CA</p>',1,223,3,'2026-04-27 19:59:36','2026-04-27 19:59:36'),(1238,'Found What We Missed','<p><strong>ΓÇ£We assumed payroll or our CPA would automatically catch this. Nope. Danna found what we missed, showed us why, and packaged it in a way that felt clean and defensible.ΓÇ¥</strong></p><p>Melissa K., Controller ΓÇö San Diego, CA</p>',1,223,3,'2026-04-27 19:59:36','2026-04-27 19:59:36'),(1239,'Tight Process','<p><strong>ΓÇ£Her process is tight: tip vs service charge separation, minimum wage threshold math, and making sure everything aligns with payroll reporting. No fluffΓÇöjust results.ΓÇ¥</strong></p><p>Derek L., Bar &amp; Lounge Operator ΓÇö San Jose, CA</p>',1,223,3,'2026-04-27 19:59:36','2026-04-27 19:59:36'),(1240,'Knows Her Craft','<p><strong>ΓÇ£Danna doesnΓÇÖt ΓÇÿkind ofΓÇÖ understand the FICA tip creditΓÇöshe knows it cold. She caught mistakes 